### IntelliJ HTTP Client examples. Community users can use curl or GraphiQL.
@portfolio = http://localhost:8081
@risk = http://localhost:8082
@accounting = http://localhost:8083

### Portfolio overview
GET {{portfolio}}/api/portfolios

### Submit an asynchronous trade (change clientKey for each new order)
POST {{portfolio}}/api/trades
Content-Type: application/json

{"clientKey":"intellij-001","portfolioId":"demo","symbol":"AAPL","side":"BUY","quantity":10,"price":185}

### Blotter
GET {{portfolio}}/api/trades

### GraphQL read
POST {{portfolio}}/graphql
Content-Type: application/json

{"query":"{ portfolios { id name cash active version } positions(id: \"demo\") { symbol quantity cost realizedPnl } }"}

### Risk decisions
GET {{risk}}/api/decisions

### Stress scenario
POST {{risk}}/api/stress
Content-Type: application/json

{"exposure":100000,"shockPercent":-15}

### Read current policy version before updating
GET {{risk}}/api/policies/default

### Update policy (replace version if it has changed)
PUT {{risk}}/api/policies/default
Content-Type: application/json

{"name":"Maximum order notional (USD)","maxNotional":100000,"version":0}

### Trial balance
GET {{accounting}}/api/trial-balance

### Immutable journals
GET {{accounting}}/api/journals

### Headers without body
HEAD {{accounting}}/api/accounts

### Discover allowed methods
OPTIONS {{risk}}/api/policies
